# lf133, the road-saying carter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf133
revision 2
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_imogen_rustford
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the road-saying carter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=carter
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk quotes_old_sayings_for_everything
likes spiced_cider old_tales old_maps warm_rain
dislikes crowds salt_wind
fears a_wheel_breaking_with_a_full_load a_well_argument_spreading_to_the_road
hopes a_clear_road_after_warm_rain a_fair_share_of_the_common_well
topics travel +0.5 work +0.4 pastimes +0.3 home +0.2
styles comfort=proverbial gossip=chatty refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# drives a #cart# along the #road#, quotes old #sayings# for every turn, and argues over a #well# no one owns.

words
oath! = Wheel and water | By the open road
saying! = A cart moves when the wheels agree | A shared well has two buckets
cart = cart | goods cart
carts = carts | loaded carts
wagon = wagon | supply wagon
wagons = wagons | supply wagons
wheel = wheel | cart wheel
wheels = wheels | cart wheels
axle = axle | wooden axle
rim = rim | wheel rim
spoke = spoke | wheel spoke
spokes = spokes | wheel spokes
harness = harness | cart harness
strap = strap | leather strap
straps = straps | leather straps
reins = reins | worn reins
load = load | goods load
loads = loads | heavy loads
sack = sack | goods sack
sacks = sacks | goods sacks
crate = crate | wooden crate
crates = crates | wooden crates
rope = rope | binding rope
knot = knot | tight knot
road = road | long road
roads = roads | drawn roads
path = path | field path
bridge = bridge | stone bridge
gate = gate | town gate
market = market | busy market
stall = stall | market stall
city = city | far city
town = town | near town
mud = mud | road mud
rut = rut | deep rut
ruts = ruts | deep ruts
stone = stone | road stone
stones = stones | road stones
map = map | old map
maps = maps | old maps
mark = mark | map mark
marks = marks | map marks
ink = ink | faded ink
tale = tale | old tale
tales = tales | road tales
story = story | travel story
stories = stories | travel stories
@2 saying = saying | old saying
sayings = sayings | old sayings
word = word | wise word
words = words | wise words
well = well | shared well
bucket = bucket | well bucket
buckets = buckets | well buckets
ropewell = ropewell | well rope
water = water | clear water
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
friend = friend | old friend
stranger = stranger | road stranger
traveller = traveller | passing traveller
merchant = merchant | road merchant
buyer = buyer | market buyer
hand = hand | cart hand
hands = hands | working hands
work = work | cart work
wage = wage | day wage
price = price | goods price
coin = coin | earned coin
watch = watch | town watch
crowd = crowd | market crowd
crowds = crowds | market crowds
salt = salt | sea salt
wind = wind | salt wind
rain = rain | warm rain
cloud = cloud | passing cloud
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | late evening
night = night | quiet night
day = day | working day
hour = hour | road hour
cider = cider | spiced cider
spice = spice | warm spice
cup = cup | cider cup
bread = bread | fresh bread
meal = meal | evening meal
table = table | shared table
house = house | shared house
home = home | cottage
door = door | front door
window = window | small window
roof = roof | sound roof
boot = boot | work boot
boots = boots | work boots
festival = festival | town festival
goods = goods | carried goods
tool = tool | wheel tool
stalls = stalls | market stalls
boards = boards | bridge boards
field = field | open field
merchants = merchants | shouting merchants
smithy = smithy | town smithy
hammer = hammer | smith hammer
winter = winter | cold winter
houses = houses | shared houses

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : The #city# gives a #cart# too many elbows and no room to turn. | I leave as soon as the #load# is off.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : The #festival# brings every #neighbour# onto the #road#. | I can hear a year's #tales# in one #day#.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A great #house# sends a #wagon# full of #goods#. | The driver still needs a fair #wage#.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : A #merchant# keeps my #cart# moving. | I read the #price# before agreeing to a #load#.
opinion @1 road for 1 : The #road# is my living; most days it takes me where I intend. | A #rut# is a problem to mend.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : A #stranger# on the #road# might need a #strap# fixed. | I ask before opening my #crates#.
opinion @1 times for 1 : Our #table# has #bread#, and the #roof# keeps out #rain#. | I can work with that.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : The #watch# knows some #roads# after dark. | I know the #ruts# it misses.
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #cart# is loaded. | #greet#. Have you heard the old #saying# about #wheels#?
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Come ride beside me to the #market#. | I have #cider# for the return.
line @1 greet.return : The #wheels# are still turning. | You found me at another #gate#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : The #house# has #bread# for you. | Come in before I start another #load#.
line @1 again.open : The #map# had led us toward its false #bridge#. | Did we reach the #well# quarrel?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #road# is calling. | Keep clear of the #cart# #wheels#.
line @1 farewell.return : Another #tale# may be waiting then. | The #well# may still belong to everyone.
line @1 react.news : Tell it while I fix this #strap#. | Did it begin on the #road#?
line @1 react.news.new : No #cart# driver has mentioned that yet. | Who saw it?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a shorter #tale# at the #gate#. | You have added the bend in the middle.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would check the #wheel# #marks#. | Which #wagon# reached the #bridge# first?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. Sit beneath the #roof#. | I will leave the #load# tied and listen.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A good #day# deserves spiced #cider#. | I will carry that news along the #road#.
line @1 answer.how : The #cart# rolled and the #harness# held. | Better since the #rain# settled the dust.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am tightening the #straps# on this #load#. | Let me turn the #cart# at the #gate#.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #road# treat your #boots# fairly? | Have you found a clean #bridge#?
line @1 sympathise : A quiet #cup# may help. | I can wait beside the #cart# while you speak.
line @1 reassure : There is another #path# on my old #map#. | We can get the #cart# moving after #rain#.
line @1 decline : I cannot carry a #load# with a broken #wheel#. | That #well# belongs to more than one #house#.
line @1 accept_decline : I heard the choice plainly; the #cart# will wait here. | Then we take the long #road#.
line @1 thank : The #axle# got checked because you kept the #reins# firm. | I needed that #cider# once the #load# was off.
line @1 deflect_thanks : The #cart# was headed that way already. | I had a spare #strap# in my #crate#.
line @1 preclose : The #wheels# need another look before dark. | The #well# will need another #bucket#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #map# sends a #cart# through a #house#. | Even my old #saying# could turn that #wheel#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #axle# is sound. | #bc_fair_enough#. The #map# deserves another look.
line @1 give.advice : Tie the #load# before the #wheels# start. | Draw from the #well# without claiming its stones.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Travel beside another #wagon# tonight. | Keep your #coin# below the #cart# seat.
scene wheel_spoke
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I tap each #spoke# before a heavy #load#. | A loose one can strand the #cart# before the #bridge#.
b : Can you hear the fault? | Can you mend it?
a : When it rings dull. | With the right #tool#.

scene harness_strap
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A frayed #strap# can slip when the #cart# turns. | I carry a spare in the #crate#.
b : Have you needed it? | How long to fit?
a : More than once. | Less than a stuck #wheel#.

scene load_knot
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I tie the #rope# so the #crates# cannot slide toward the #wheel#. | The #knot# has to open when we unload.
b : Do you test it? | Who taught you?
a : With a hard pull. | Too many wet #roads#.

scene market_turn
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #market# #road# narrows between two #stalls#. | I arrive before the #crowd# can close it.
b : Does that help? | What if you are late?
a : Every time. | I take the far #gate#.

scene bridge_weight
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #bridge# sounds different under an empty #cart# and a full one. | I slow before its middle.
b : Are you afraid of it? | Do others slow?
a : I respect its #boards#. | The careful drivers.

scene deep_rut
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #rut# can hold one #wheel# while the other rolls on. | I carry #stones# to give it a firm edge.
b : Does that free it? | Who helps?
a : With a push. | A passing #hand#.

scene wrong_map
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My old #map# draws a #road# through a marsh where I find a #field#. | Its false #roads# have given me plenty of #stories#.
b : Have you followed it? | Will you correct it?
a : Once. | I like it wrong.

scene old_saying
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An old #saying# suits a #cart# even when it does not suit the weather. | I try one for each bad turn.
b : Do you make them up? | Do they help?
a : I borrow most. | They fill the #hour#.

scene spiced_cider
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Spiced #cider# tastes best after a long #road# without #rain#. | I keep a #cup# for when the #cart# is unloaded.
b : Do you make it? | Do you share?
a : Someone else does. | With a #friend#.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Warm #rain# settles the #road# dust before making the #ruts# soft. | I use the first hour to finish a #load#.
b : Does that work? | Do you like rain?
a : If I move quickly. | At its beginning.

scene salt_wind
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #salt# #wind# reaches the #road# and makes the #reins# stiff. | I prefer the local #rain#.
b : Does it come often? | Can you cover the load?
a : Too often. | With canvas.

scene well_bucket
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The shared #well# has room for two #buckets# if we take turns. | A #neighbour# says it belongs to one #house#.
b : Do you agree? | Who settles it?
a : The #well# serves both houses. | We should.

scene well_quarrel
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I have argued over a #well# that neither side built. | The #water# keeps coming while we speak.
b : Have you made peace? | Why does it matter?
a : Not yet. | Every #bucket# matters.

scene crowded_road
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #crowd# leaving the #festival# can stop a #cart# longer than #mud#. | I take the outer #road#.
b : Does it add distance? | Do you enjoy the festival?
a : A little. | After the #load#.

scene city_delivery
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #city# makes me unload among shouting #merchants#. | I count every #crate# before turning home.
b : Do they pay? | Would you stay?
a : After the count. | Not willingly.

scene housemate_iron
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #house# shares a roof with a #smithy# worker. | I hear the #hammer# before my #cart# leaves.
b : Does that wake you? | Do you ask for repairs?
a : Often. | When a #rim# bends.

scene road_tale
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An old #tale# can make a long #road# feel shorter. | I tell it to whoever rides beside the #load#.
b : Do they believe it? | Do you tell it again?
a : Some. | Every #winter#.

story shared_well [topic=home self.age>=18]
  : My #neighbour# claimed the #well# while I was filling a #bucket#.
  : I asked who had built it; neither of us knew.
  b : A difficult quarrel. Did you take the water?
  : We drew a #bucket# each.

story wrong_turn [topic=travel self.age>=18]
  : I trusted an old #map# and turned the #cart# toward a missing #bridge#.
  : The real #road# bent past a #field#.
  b : A poor map. Did you turn back?
  : I did, and kept the map for its tale.

story spoke_before_bridge [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : A #wheel# #spoke# sounded dull before I crossed the #bridge#.
  : I stopped and tightened it beside the #road#.
  ask : Did it hold?
  b : Good listening.
  : Through the rest of the journey.

rule @bark_wheel
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That #spoke# sounds loose. | Check the #rim# before loading.

rule @bark_saying
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say A #cart# needs two sound #wheels#. | That #saying# fits today.

rule @bark_well
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say One #bucket# each at the #well#. | The #water# belongs to both #houses#.

rule @bark_map
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say The #bridge# is drawn in the wrong place. | This #map# still amuses me.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. The #cart# is nearly loaded. | #greet#. I have a #saying# for this #road#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : The #wheel# held since you last rode. | The #well# argument has not ended.
dlg @1 resident.job : I drive a #cart# from #self.workplace#. | I tie #loads#, count #crates#, and mend #straps#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. The #road# is waiting. | #saying.capitalize#. Mind the #wheels#.
graft resident.hub
choice Who owns the well? -> well
node well
say No one can show who built it. We should draw #water# by turns.
free
choice Why keep a wrong map? -> map
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node map
say Its wrong #bridge# gave me a good #story# for the #road#.
choice Back to the cart. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #harness# is set. | #greet#. The #road# has room for this #cart# today.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will check the #axle#. | The #cider# can wait until home.
